{
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {"name":"pymapper","version":"<version>","informationUri":"https://github.com/pymapper/pymapper","rules":[
          {"id":"PM101","name":"complex-function","shortDescription":{"text":"Function with a McCabe cyclomatic complexity above `max-mccabe`"},"help":{"text":"McCabe complexity counts the independent paths through a function, exactly as ruff's C901 / PyCQA mccabe: 1, plus one per `if`, `elif`, `for`, `while`, `except` handler, `try`-`else`, nested function and `match` case (minus one when the last case is an irrefutable, unguarded pattern). Boolean operators, conditional expressions, comprehensions, `with` and `assert` are not counted. High values mean many paths to test and reason about.\n\nFix: extract branches into well-named helpers, replace `if`/`elif` chains with a dispatch table, or return early.","markdown":"McCabe complexity counts the independent paths through a function, exactly as ruff's C901 / PyCQA mccabe: 1, plus one per `if`, `elif`, `for`, `while`, `except` handler, `try`-`else`, nested function and `match` case (minus one when the last case is an irrefutable, unguarded pattern). Boolean operators, conditional expressions, comprehensions, `with` and `assert` are not counted. High values mean many paths to test and reason about.\n\nFix: extract branches into well-named helpers, replace `if`/`elif` chains with a dispatch table, or return early."},"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"properties":{"category":"Complexity and size","cost":"O(n)"}},
          {"id":"PM106","name":"low-maintainability","shortDescription":{"text":"Function with a maintainability index below `min-maintainability`"},"help":{"text":"Maintainability index on a 0-100 scale: `clamp((171 - 5.2 ln V - 0.23 CC - 16.2 ln LOC) * 100 / 171, 0, 100)`, where V is the Halstead volume, CC the McCabe complexity and LOC the line count. It blends size and complexity into one number and is best used to rank code, which is why the rule is off by default.\n\nFix: reduce the function's size and complexity (see PM101 and PM104).","markdown":"Maintainability index on a 0-100 scale: `clamp((171 - 5.2 ln V - 0.23 CC - 16.2 ln LOC) * 100 / 171, 0, 100)`, where V is the Halstead volume, CC the McCabe complexity and LOC the line count. It blends size and complexity into one number and is best used to rank code, which is why the rule is off by default.\n\nFix: reduce the function's size and complexity (see PM101 and PM104)."},"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"note"},"properties":{"category":"Complexity and size","cost":"O(n)"}},
          {"id":"PM107","name":"long-module","shortDescription":{"text":"Module longer than `max-module-loc` lines, docstrings excluded"},"help":{"text":"Lines of the module file minus the lines of every docstring in it (the module's, and those of its classes and functions, as for PM104). Blank lines and comments count. Very long modules are hard to navigate and usually hold several unrelated concerns.\n\nFix: split the module into a package of focused modules.","markdown":"Lines of the module file minus the lines of every docstring in it (the module's, and those of its classes and functions, as for PM104). Blank lines and comments count. Very long modules are hard to navigate and usually hold several unrelated concerns.\n\nFix: split the module into a package of focused modules."},"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"note"},"properties":{"category":"Complexity and size","cost":"O(n)"}},
          {"id":"PM301","name":"import-cycle","shortDescription":{"text":"Modules that import each other, directly or indirectly"},"help":{"text":"One finding per strongly connected component of the first-party module import graph, reported at an import that closes a short witness cycle. The message gives the number of modules in the component and the witness, ending at the first module again; JSON output adds a `cycle` object with the component's `size`, every `member` and the `witness`. Cycles make import order matter, cause `ImportError`s on partially initialised modules and prevent splitting code into independent parts. Imports under `if TYPE_CHECKING:` are ignored unless `analysis.type-checking-cycles` is set; function-level imports count, stub files (`.pyi`) do not.\n\nFix: move the shared code into a lower-level module both can import, or invert the dependency.","markdown":"One finding per strongly connected component of the first-party module import graph, reported at an import that closes a short witness cycle. The message gives the number of modules in the component and the witness, ending at the first module again; JSON output adds a `cycle` object with the component's `size`, every `member` and the `witness`. Cycles make import order matter, cause `ImportError`s on partially initialised modules and prevent splitting code into independent parts. Imports under `if TYPE_CHECKING:` are ignored unless `analysis.type-checking-cycles` is set; function-level imports count, stub files (`.pyi`) do not.\n\nFix: move the shared code into a lower-level module both can import, or invert the dependency."},"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"properties":{"category":"Import cycles and layering","cost":"O(V+E)"}},
          {"id":"PM303","name":"forbidden-import","shortDescription":{"text":"Import breaking a `forbidden` contract"},"help":{"text":"A `kind = \"forbidden\"` contract forbids its `source` modules (and their submodules) from importing its `forbidden` modules, which may be first- or third-party. Modules that are not analysed match unresolved imports by dotted prefix. Reported at each violating import; with `transitive = true` also at imports that lead to a forbidden module through modules outside the contract. Stub files (`.pyi`) are not checked.\n\nFix: remove the dependency, or move the code that needs it out of the source modules.","markdown":"A `kind = \"forbidden\"` contract forbids its `source` modules (and their submodules) from importing its `forbidden` modules, which may be first- or third-party. Modules that are not analysed match unresolved imports by dotted prefix. Reported at each violating import; with `transitive = true` also at imports that lead to a forbidden module through modules outside the contract. Stub files (`.pyi`) are not checked.\n\nFix: remove the dependency, or move the code that needs it out of the source modules."},"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"properties":{"category":"Import cycles and layering","cost":"O(V+E)"}},
          {"id":"PM401","name":"unused-function","shortDescription":{"text":"Module-level or nested function that is never used"},"help":{"text":"The function is not reachable from any root: nothing live calls it, references it, re-exports it or registers it (decorator entry points, presets).\n\nFix: delete it, or declare how it is used (`[entrypoints]`, a preset, `__all__`).","markdown":"The function is not reachable from any root: nothing live calls it, references it, re-exports it or registers it (decorator entry points, presets).\n\nFix: delete it, or declare how it is used (`[entrypoints]`, a preset, `__all__`)."},"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"properties":{"category":"Dead code","cost":"O(V+E)"}},
          {"id":"PM405","name":"unused-import","shortDescription":{"text":"Import that neither its module nor any importer of that module uses"},"help":{"text":"Unlike per-file linters, this also follows re-exports: an import counts as used when another module imports the name from here or accesses it as `module.name`. Imports listed in `__all__`, the `import x as x` idiom, `__init__.py` re-exports in library mode, star imports, `__future__` imports and `try`/`except ImportError` fallbacks are kept.\n\nFix: delete the import, or add the name to `__all__` if it is part of the module's API.","markdown":"Unlike per-file linters, this also follows re-exports: an import counts as used when another module imports the name from here or accesses it as `module.name`. Imports listed in `__all__`, the `import x as x` idiom, `__init__.py` re-exports in library mode, star imports, `__future__` imports and `try`/`except ImportError` fallbacks are kept.\n\nFix: delete the import, or add the name to `__all__` if it is part of the module's API."},"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"properties":{"category":"Dead code","cost":"O(V+E)"}},
          {"id":"PM501","name":"duplicate-code","shortDescription":{"text":"Block of code duplicated elsewhere (token-based clone)"},"help":{"text":"Token sequences of at least `dupes-min-tokens` tokens spanning at least `dupes-min-lines` lines that occur more than once, after normalising identifiers and literals (so renamed copies match). Reported at each copy, pointing at another copy; JSON output adds the copy's `end_line`, its `symbol` (the innermost class or function containing the whole copy, if any) and an `other` object with the other copy's `path`, `line`, `end_line` and `symbol`. Import statements are ignored, stub files (`.pyi`) are skipped, and a copy never starts or ends on an `@overload` signature or a docstring (it is trimmed to the code in between, and dropped if too little is left), so runs of overloads are not reported. Duplicates must be kept in sync by hand and drift apart.\n\nFix: extract the shared code into a function or base class.\n\nOff unless `analysis.dupes = true` (token-window hashing across all first-party files).","markdown":"Token sequences of at least `dupes-min-tokens` tokens spanning at least `dupes-min-lines` lines that occur more than once, after normalising identifiers and literals (so renamed copies match). Reported at each copy, pointing at another copy; JSON output adds the copy's `end_line`, its `symbol` (the innermost class or function containing the whole copy, if any) and an `other` object with the other copy's `path`, `line`, `end_line` and `symbol`. Import statements are ignored, stub files (`.pyi`) are skipped, and a copy never starts or ends on an `@overload` signature or a docstring (it is trimmed to the code in between, and dropped if too little is left), so runs of overloads are not reported. Duplicates must be kept in sync by hand and drift apart.\n\nFix: extract the shared code into a function or base class.\n\nOff unless `analysis.dupes = true` (token-window hashing across all first-party files)."},"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"note"},"properties":{"category":"Duplication","cost":"expensive"}},
          {"id":"PM601","name":"undeclared-dependency","shortDescription":{"text":"Import of a third-party distribution not declared in `pyproject.toml`"},"help":{"text":"First-party code imports a module whose distribution is not listed in `[project.dependencies]`, `[project.optional-dependencies]`, a `[dependency-groups]` group or the poetry / uv / pdm dependency tables of the `pyproject.toml` that applies to the file (its nearest project unit that declares dependencies). The code works only because the package happens to be installed. What a declared meta-package (installed, no importable name) requires directly counts as declared. Units whose `dependencies` are `dynamic` are not checked.\n\nFix: add the distribution to the project's dependencies.","markdown":"First-party code imports a module whose distribution is not listed in `[project.dependencies]`, `[project.optional-dependencies]`, a `[dependency-groups]` group or the poetry / uv / pdm dependency tables of the `pyproject.toml` that applies to the file (its nearest project unit that declares dependencies). The code works only because the package happens to be installed. What a declared meta-package (installed, no importable name) requires directly counts as declared. Units whose `dependencies` are `dynamic` are not checked.\n\nFix: add the distribution to the project's dependencies."},"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"properties":{"category":"Dependencies","cost":"O(n)"}},
          {"id":"PM602","name":"unused-dependency","shortDescription":{"text":"Declared dependency that no first-party module imports"},"help":{"text":"A distribution in `[project.dependencies]` (or poetry's main dependencies) provides no module that the unit's first-party code imports. Optional and development groups are not checked. A distribution that installs no importable name (a command-line tool, a meta-package) is reported with confidence 50. Plugins, CLI tools and runtime-only extras are legitimate exceptions; ignore them with `per-file-ignores` on `pyproject.toml` or an inline suppression on the dependency line.\n\nFix: remove the dependency, or move it to the group that needs it.","markdown":"A distribution in `[project.dependencies]` (or poetry's main dependencies) provides no module that the unit's first-party code imports. Optional and development groups are not checked. A distribution that installs no importable name (a command-line tool, a meta-package) is reported with confidence 50. Plugins, CLI tools and runtime-only extras are legitimate exceptions; ignore them with `per-file-ignores` on `pyproject.toml` or an inline suppression on the dependency line.\n\nFix: remove the dependency, or move it to the group that needs it."},"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"properties":{"category":"Dependencies","cost":"O(n)"}}
        ]}
      },
      "columnKind": "unicodeCodePoints",
      "results": [
        {"ruleId":"PM301","ruleIndex":3,"level":"warning","message":{"text":"import cycle (2 modules): pkg.alpha -> pkg.zeta -> pkg.alpha"},"partialFingerprints":{"pymapperKey/v1":"abfc58f9fcb8502b"},"properties":{"confidence":100}},
        {"ruleId":"PM602","ruleIndex":9,"level":"warning","message":{"text":"dependency `requests` is declared but never imported"},"partialFingerprints":{"pymapperKey/v1":"4fdec368f5c79095"},"properties":{"confidence":100}},
        {"ruleId":"PM401","ruleIndex":5,"level":"warning","message":{"text":"function `odd:f` is never used"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"odd%20dir/a%2Cb%3Ac%25d%22e.py","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"startLine":1,"startColumn":1}},"logicalLocations":[{"fullyQualifiedName":"odd:f"}]}],"partialFingerprints":{"pymapperKey/v1":"9950404ea4a5bc3f"},"properties":{"confidence":60}},
        {"ruleId":"PM107","ruleIndex":2,"level":"note","message":{"text":"module `pkg` is 900 lines long without docstrings (> 500)"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"pkg/__init__.py","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"}},"logicalLocations":[{"fullyQualifiedName":"pkg"}]}],"partialFingerprints":{"pymapperKey/v1":"50bbc5c7407a7145"},"properties":{"confidence":100}},
        {"ruleId":"PM303","ruleIndex":4,"level":"error","message":{"text":"`pkg.alpha` imports forbidden module `we\"ird\nname` (contract `core-layers`)"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"pkg/alpha.py","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"startLine":3,"startColumn":1}},"logicalLocations":[{"fullyQualifiedName":"pkg.alpha"}]}],"partialFingerprints":{"pymapperKey/v1":"48a4a6d935b1c3ff"},"properties":{"confidence":100}},
        {"ruleId":"PM405","ruleIndex":6,"level":"warning","message":{"text":"`os.path` is imported but never used"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"pkg/alpha.py","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"startLine":3,"startColumn":1}},"logicalLocations":[{"fullyQualifiedName":"pkg.alpha:os.path"}]}],"partialFingerprints":{"pymapperKey/v1":"4a08a08acf6504f5"},"properties":{"confidence":90}},
        {"ruleId":"PM405","ruleIndex":6,"level":"warning","message":{"text":"`yaml` is imported but never used"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"pkg/alpha.py","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"startLine":3,"startColumn":1}},"logicalLocations":[{"fullyQualifiedName":"pkg.alpha:yaml"}]}],"partialFingerprints":{"pymapperKey/v1":"7b24408f6a8a832b"},"properties":{"confidence":90}},
        {"ruleId":"PM106","ruleIndex":1,"level":"note","message":{"text":"`pkg.alpha:Big.run` has a low maintainability index (12.2 < 20.0)"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"pkg/alpha.py","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"startLine":20,"startColumn":5}},"logicalLocations":[{"fullyQualifiedName":"pkg.alpha:Big.run"}]}],"partialFingerprints":{"pymapperKey/v1":"602726420d5802f9"},"properties":{"confidence":100}},
        {"ruleId":"PM601","ruleIndex":8,"level":"error","message":{"text":"`yaml` is provided by `PyYAML`, which is not a declared dependency"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"pkg/caf%C3%A9/%EF%BF%BD.py","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"startLine":2}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"pymapperKey/v1":"ad21086ada72cb65"},"properties":{"confidence":100}},
        {"ruleId":"PM101","ruleIndex":0,"level":"warning","message":{"text":"`pkg.zeta:handle` is too complex (McCabe 14 > 10)"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"pkg/zeta.py","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"startLine":12,"startColumn":5}},"logicalLocations":[{"fullyQualifiedName":"pkg.zeta:handle"}]}],"partialFingerprints":{"pymapperKey/v1":"7f51e8bd9937449d"},"properties":{"confidence":100}},
        {"ruleId":"PM501","ruleIndex":7,"level":"note","message":{"text":"8 lines duplicated in pkg/alpha.py:40"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"pkg/zeta.py","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"startLine":14,"startColumn":9}},"logicalLocations":[{"fullyQualifiedName":"pkg.zeta:handle"}]}],"partialFingerprints":{"pymapperKey/v1":"0a6e6e3f473097fa"},"properties":{"confidence":96}}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
